{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "framework-nano-fd-av",
      "prompt": "Run ONE Cosmos3 action forward-dynamics rollout with the cosmos_framework inference path on this machine's single GPU. Use a fresh clone of the public framework repository, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git (branch main), as the framework checkout and set it up per the skill; run the AV forward-dynamics example with Cosmos3-Nano (guardrails disabled, seed 0) from the entry skill's bundled start frame (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/images/av_0.jpg) and forward ego trajectory (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/actions/av_traj_forward.json); save the generated video as outputs/fd_av_framework.mp4 and the JSONL input spec you ran as outputs/fd_av_framework_spec.jsonl.",
      "expected_outcome": "The framework inference completes on one GPU with Cosmos3-Nano from a fresh clone of the public framework main and a 61-frame, 10 fps AV rollout exists as outputs/fd_av_framework.mp4; result_summary.md records the exact command, the runtime and the decoded stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "Inference ran through cosmos_framework.scripts.inference with --parallelism-preset=latency, --checkpoint-path Cosmos3-Nano and --image_size 480, in the documented single-process form (MASTER_ADDR/MASTER_PORT/RANK/WORLD_SIZE/LOCAL_RANK) or the README's torchrun --nproc-per-node=1 form",
        "The framework checkout used for setup and inference is a fresh clone of the public NVIDIA/cosmos-framework main (the transcript shows the clone), not the skill snapshot",
        "A JSONL forward-dynamics spec with model_mode forward_dynamics, domain_name av, action_chunk_size 60, fps 10 and absolute paths to the bundled av_0.jpg and av_traj_forward.json was written and passed with -i",
        "outputs/fd_av_framework.mp4 exists, is a valid non-empty video of 61 frames at 10 fps (decoder facts in the transcript) and is the vision.mp4 this run wrote, not copied from elsewhere or fabricated",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md contains the exact command line used, the measured runtime and the GPU memory observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_framework.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_framework_spec.jsonl",
          "contains": "forward_dynamics"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "spec build",
        "inference run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "diffusers-nano-fd-av",
      "prompt": "Run ONE Cosmos3 action forward-dynamics rollout with the diffusers path on this machine's single GPU: the av_forward case, Cosmos3-Nano in bf16 with the bundled AV start frame (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/images/av_0.jpg) and forward ego trajectory (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/actions/av_traj_forward.json), guardrails disabled (the notebook default); save the generated video as outputs/fd_av_diffusers.mp4 and record its resolution, frame count and fps in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "A 61-frame, 10 fps AV rollout generated by Cosmos3-Nano through Cosmos3OmniPipeline with a CosmosActionCondition exists as outputs/fd_av_diffusers.mp4, and result_summary.md records model, settings, runtime, peak CUDA memory and the stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "A dedicated Python environment was created for diffusers per the skill (uv venv plus the documented install list) and the generation ran from it, not the system python",
        "nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano was loaded in bfloat16 and the rollout used CosmosActionCondition with mode forward_dynamics, domain_name av, chunk_size 60 and resolution_tier 480, with the documented sampling (30 steps, guidance 1.0, flow shift 10.0, use_system_prompt False, seed 0)",
        "outputs/fd_av_diffusers.mp4 exists, is a valid non-empty MP4 of 61 frames at 10 fps, and was produced by the pipeline run recorded in the transcript (not copied or fabricated)",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md reports the settings, wall-clock time, GPU memory and stream facts actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_diffusers.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "env setup",
        "model load",
        "rollout",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trtllm-nano-fd-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with TensorRT-LLM (trtllm-serve with the one-GPU Nano VisualGen config, guardrails disabled) and run ONE action forward-dynamics request through its synchronous video API: the AV example from the bundled start frame (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/images/av_0.jpg) and forward ego trajectory (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/actions/av_traj_forward.json). Save the returned tensor payload as outputs/fd_av_trtllm.safetensors and the rollout decoded from it as outputs/fd_av_trtllm.mp4, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "trtllm-serve hosts Cosmos3-Nano on one GPU, one forward-dynamics request returns a safetensors payload with video, action and frame_rate tensors, and the decoded 61-frame rollout plus summary and transcript are in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "trtllm-serve was launched for nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with the cosmos3-nano-1gpu.yaml visual_gen_args and /health answered before the request was sent",
        "Guardrails were disabled via the documented mechanism (TRTLLM_DISABLE_COSMOS3_GUARDRAILS=1 or use_guardrails false in extra_params) rather than by acquiring gated access",
        "The request was a multipart POST /v1/videos/sync with format=safetensors, response_format=file, the AV prompt, extra_params action_mode forward_dynamics / domain_name av / the 60x9 trajectory, and av_0.jpg uploaded as image_reference",
        "outputs/fd_av_trtllm.safetensors holds video, action and frame_rate tensors and outputs/fd_av_trtllm.mp4 is the 61-frame rollout decoded from it (shapes printed in the transcript), neither copied nor fabricated",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records the serve command, readiness time, request latency and the tensor shapes"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_trtllm.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_trtllm.safetensors",
          "min_bytes": 1000000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server install + start",
        "readiness",
        "forward-dynamics request",
        "decode + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-nano-fd-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with vLLM-Omni (the skill's documented Docker launch, guardrails disabled) and run ONE action forward-dynamics request through its video API: the AV example from the bundled start frame (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/images/av_0.jpg) and forward ego trajectory (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/actions/av_traj_forward.json). Save the returned rollout as outputs/fd_av_vllm.mp4 and the server's final job JSON as outputs/fd_av_vllm_final.json, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server comes up, serves one forward-dynamics request from the bundled AV inputs, and a 61-frame, 10 fps rollout plus the job JSON, summary and transcript exist in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the documented image, flags and --no-guardrails, and /v1/models returned model metadata before any request",
        "The request was a multipart POST /v1/videos with av_0.jpg as input_reference, num_frames 61, fps 10, size equal to the start frame, the documented sampling (30 steps, guidance 1.0, flow shift 10.0) and extra_params action_mode forward_dynamics / domain_name av / action_chunk_size 60 / image_size 480 / the 60x9 trajectory",
        "The job was polled on GET /v1/videos/{id} until status completed and the video downloaded from /content; outputs/fd_av_vllm.mp4 is a valid non-empty 61-frame video (not copied or fabricated)",
        "The server was stopped and cleaned up at the end",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready and request latency"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_vllm.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_vllm_final.json",
          "contains": "completed"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "forward-dynamics request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-nano-fd-av",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano with SGLang (the skill's documented Docker launch) and run ONE action forward-dynamics request through its video API: the AV example from the bundled start frame (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/images/av_0.jpg) and forward ego trajectory (../cosmos3-inference-action/assets/actions/av_traj_forward.json). Save the returned rollout as outputs/fd_av_sglang.mp4 and the server's final job JSON as outputs/fd_av_sglang_final.json, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "The SGLang server comes up, serves one forward-dynamics request from the bundled AV inputs, and a 61-frame, 10 fps rollout plus the job JSON, summary and transcript exist in artifacts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The SGLang server was started with the documented image and flags, and /v1/models returned model metadata before any request",
        "The request was a multipart POST /v1/videos with av_0.jpg as input_reference, num_frames 61, fps 10, size equal to the start frame, the documented sampling (30 steps, guidance 1.0, flow shift 10.0) and extra_params action_mode forward_dynamics / domain_name av / action_view_point ego_view / the 60x9 trajectory / guardrails false",
        "The job was polled on GET /v1/videos/{id} until status completed and the video downloaded from /content; outputs/fd_av_sglang.mp4 is a valid non-empty 61-frame video (not copied or fabricated)",
        "The server was stopped and cleaned up at the end",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready and request latency"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/fd_av_sglang_final.json",
          "contains": "completed"
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "forward-dynamics request",
        "teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN",
    "GITHUB_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
